From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] adaptive: keep uniform decode graphs alongside varlen decode

Measured on PP6 (DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, DSpark K=5, max_num_seqs=32, SM80): with
adaptive verification enabled but nothing actually trimmed, a step of 6 requests
x 6 verification rows ran the 40-row graph, i.e. it did 11% more verification
work than the step asked for. Counting throughput was 12-15% below the same
build with the feature off, at unchanged acceptance (5.952 of 6) and unchanged
real row count (36).

Cause: CudaGraphManager._init_candidates treats the two decode capture strategies
as alternatives. varlen_decode is set whenever the adaptive manager exists, and
the uniform-decode branch hung off that test as `elif ... and not
self.varlen_decode`, so with the feature on the only decode graphs available were
the varlen buckets - [1,2,4] plus multiples of 8 - which do not contain 6x6=36.
Any uniform step whose row count is not also a multiple of 8 is padded up to the
next bucket. Enabling the feature therefore costs work even on steps it decides
not to trim.

Fix: capture uniform decode graphs alongside the varlen set, for the row counts
no varlen bucket covers exactly (17 new graphs in this configuration, 36 among
them). Two guards keep this from hurting anything:

  * they are prepended to the candidate lists instead of joining the range
    partitioning, because a uniform graph inserted into the partitioning would
    claim every row count below its bucket and starve ragged steps of their
    varlen graph; and
  * a uniform graph is prepended to a row count only when it is strictly smaller
    than the smallest FULL graph already covering it, so exact buckets (24, 48,
    96) and near-exact ones (30 -> 32 rows, 2 rows of padding) keep their
    existing graphs rather than being bumped to a larger uniform fit.

Dispatch is otherwise unchanged: _is_compatible() still refuses a uniform graph
unless the step is uniform at exactly that width, so ragged and mixed steps
resolve exactly as before. Simulated over all 192 reachable decode row counts
for both uniform and ragged steps: 17 counts improve to zero padding, 0 regress.

Signed-off-by: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py
@@ -261,6 +261,12 @@
         capture_varlen_decode = (
             separate_decode_routine and bool(decode_mode) and self.varlen_decode
         )
+        # Uniform decode graphs are captured ALONGSIDE the varlen set rather than
+        # replacing it. Varlen buckets are multiples of 8 above 8, so a full-budget
+        # step of 6 reqs x 6 rows = 36 has no 36-row graph and pads up to 40,
+        # verifying 11% more rows than it asked for - on a step where adaptive
+        # verification trimmed nothing at all.
+        uniform_decode_descs: list[BatchExecutionDescriptor] = []
         for num_tokens, num_active_loras in product(
             capture_sizes, self.lora_capture_cases
         ):
@@ -275,9 +281,12 @@
                     num_active_loras=num_active_loras,
                 )
                 descs_by_mode[decode_mode].append(desc)
-            # Capture uniform decode specfifc graphs if required
-            #  (i.e. separate decode routine)
-            elif separate_decode_routine and decode_mode and not self.varlen_decode:
+            # Capture uniform decode specific graphs if required
+            #  (i.e. separate decode routine). Deliberately an independent `if`,
+            # never an `elif` on the varlen branch: under varlen every bucket at
+            # or below max_decode_tokens takes the varlen path first, so an `elif`
+            # here would not run for exactly the sizes that need it.
+            if separate_decode_routine and decode_mode:
                 for decode_query_len in decode_query_lens:
                     rounded_num_tokens = round_up(num_tokens, decode_query_len)
                     rounded_num_reqs = rounded_num_tokens // decode_query_len
@@ -298,7 +307,17 @@
                     )
 
                     # avoid duplicate graphs
-                    if desc not in descs_by_mode[decode_mode]:
+                    if capture_varlen_decode:
+                        # A varlen graph of the same row count already serves a
+                        # uniform step with zero padding, so only row counts that
+                        # would otherwise be rounded up need a uniform graph.
+                        if (
+                            rounded_num_tokens
+                            not in {d.num_tokens for d in descs_by_mode[decode_mode]}
+                            and desc not in uniform_decode_descs
+                        ):
+                            uniform_decode_descs.append(desc)
+                    elif desc not in descs_by_mode[decode_mode]:
                         descs_by_mode[decode_mode].append(desc)
 
             # recoverSSM cannot capture a dummy query wider than its workspace.
@@ -326,6 +345,44 @@
             descs.sort(key=lambda d: d.num_tokens, reverse=True)
             self._capture_descs[mode] = descs
 
+        if uniform_decode_descs:
+            # Capture them, but keep them out of the range partitioning that
+            # follows: a uniform graph inserted there would claim the row counts
+            # under its bucket and starve ragged steps of their varlen graph,
+            # dropping those steps to eager. Each one is instead prepended only to
+            # the row counts it can serve, and _is_compatible() already refuses a
+            # uniform graph unless the step is uniform at exactly that width.
+            captured = self._capture_descs[decode_mode]
+            captured.extend(uniform_decode_descs)
+            captured.sort(key=lambda d: d.num_tokens, reverse=True)
+            # Descending size, inserting at the head, so the TIGHTEST fitting
+            # uniform graph ends up first: dispatch returns the first compatible
+            # candidate, and a uniform graph is compatible with any uniform step
+            # whose row count is one of its multiples.
+            for uniform_desc in sorted(
+                uniform_decode_descs, key=lambda d: -d.num_tokens
+            ):
+                width = uniform_desc.uniform_token_count
+                assert width is not None
+                for rows in range(width, uniform_desc.num_tokens + 1, width):
+                    key = (rows, uniform_desc.num_active_loras)
+                    candidates = self._candidates.setdefault(key, [])
+                    # Only outrank an existing FULL graph when this one is
+                    # strictly smaller, i.e. pads less. Varlen buckets are
+                    # multiples of 8, so 24/48/96 are already exact and 30 is
+                    # covered by the 32-row graph with 2 rows of padding - a
+                    # uniform-36 graph would pad that to 6, so it must not
+                    # displace them.
+                    covered_by = [
+                        desc.num_tokens
+                        for desc in candidates
+                        if desc.cg_mode == decode_mode
+                    ]
+                    if covered_by and uniform_desc.num_tokens >= min(covered_by):
+                        continue
+                    if uniform_desc not in candidates:
+                        candidates.insert(0, uniform_desc)
+
         for mode in (CUDAGraphMode.FULL, CUDAGraphMode.PIECEWISE):
             mode_descs = tuple(reversed(descs_by_mode.get(mode, [])))
             for num_active_loras in self.lora_capture_cases:
